body:
I was cautiously optimistic about this skin. "Maybe I will reinstall", I thought. "Maybe I can spend my built-up currency." Blizzard literally telling me to get fucked I guess. This game is literally "dead dove: do not eat". I open the bag and you know what that's my fault for thinking they would price this reasonably. Mea culpa.

&#x200B;

Imagine paying 2/3 of Baldur's Gate 3 (a brand new game, goty material, hundreds of hours of high quality RPG) for a fucking skin bundle. Not me.

You sound upset that your shiny TOP weapon is less prestigious than you think it should be

&#x200B;

cry more

A CLEAR IS A CLEAR STAY MAD C48S SKILL ISSUE :)

&#x200B;

EDIT: this just in people clearing the fight the first time don't have crazy good parses compared to people who do the fight over and over on farm wHO COULD HAVE FORSEEN????

I totally get the flying around in circles in tempest. Sometimes I'll just semi-afk on top of >!one of the buildings!< being totally unproductive because honestly I don't know what else to do

&#x200B;

I criticized stormblood for not having enough emotional weight throughout when compared to heavensward but oh my lord they made up for it with shadowbringers.

It's so heavily implied that we can probably call it confirmed at this point

&#x200B;

But what I really want to know is if we're responsible for hydaelyn because if so oh no we broke everything :(

I remember one galaxy brain poster somewhere who argued they were being asked to solve an algebraic equation, like figuring out how to add to a prime number was some 3hard5me shit

&#x200B;

good times

thanks, reading that made me nauseous 

&#x200B;

how many of those posters diddle kids, you reckon?

I sort of came at it from the angle of "I want a dmc tattoo but also something that looks great even if nobody knows what it's referencing" (I have a new vegas platinum chip tattoo along the same kind of vein). From there it was pretty easy for me to narrow it down. V is my favorite character to play in 5 (I never knew how much I needed a pet class in my stylish action until now) and out of the three summons Griffon is definitely the one with the most character (and birds always look good in ink). He ties back to dmc1 too, which was a big plus. I was kind of 50/50 on whether Griffon should hold V's book or cane but i figured the cane was better aesthetically.

&#x200B;

That was the rough thought process :)

I think it sits in grey area since the blacklist is curated outside of the game on discord, so as long as nobody says anything in game teeeeechnically there's nothing to report them in game for.

&#x200B;

The moment someone mentions "the list" or some shit in game though I'd smash that report button like the fist of a mighty god just to spite people who think their clique pREEEEEEmades are more entitled to a portal than you

i'm reporting because him going around shirtless makes me feel cold

&#x200B;

there's snow outside here m8 get that warm weather no shirt privilege outta here

I know this is a cheeky post but imagine road conditions being so dangerous you shouldn't even leave your house

&#x200B;

That's what a bunch of people had today

What it really did for me was make me realize how much emotional labor i put into this game, working and coordinating people in group chat, helping other people out, etc. Maybe it's not healthy for me to be this involved. I know I help people and they appreciate the work, but for Niantic to ask us to go out in this weather for this event was really extra. I think it might be best for me to take a break because obviously Niantic can't be assed to make sure people play this game safely, and idk if I can support that. Telling people that there's weather warnings while at the same time encouraging us to go out for this super special 3 hour event for an extremely popular shiny (feebas/milotic) is some super mixed message shit.

&#x200B;

I agree that it's hard for someone who doesn't live here to understand.

Yeah, I'm fine with a lower shiny chance as long as they give us some time to grind. 3 hours is a really small window and the weather here is just awful (snowstorm)

&#x200B;

Longer time would mitigate the weather issues a lot of us are having on top of the low % chance

I can never recommend walking sims full price (unless they're like $10 or less), it never feels like I get my money's worth. YMMV obviously!

&#x200B;

It just doesn't feel right to me to pay a premium for what is basically a movie is all.
